after returning to the modern era and  the cold war call of duty is headed back  to world war ii with sledgehammer's next  entry in the series call of duty  vanguard is both a broader and a more  specific look at the conflict  sledgehammer is telling a story that  will take you across several fronts and  show you four different perspectives  culminating in the creation of the first  special forces a development that will  change how wars are waged forever  gamespot got an early hands-off look at  vanguard which gave us a whole lot of  information about the game note that we  couldn't capture video from the event so  a lot of what you're seeing here is  footage from call of duty world war ii  if you want more call of duty coverage  be sure to hit like and subscribe  to start with sledgehammer studios head  aaron halon acknowledged the stories of  employee harassment and discrimination  from the state of california's recent  lawsuit against activision blizzard head  to gamespot.com for full coverage about  the lawsuit how activision has responded  what employees have said about working  there and all the latest news about the  situation  the presentation then dug into  vanguard's campaign which focuses on the  birth of special forces which means  taking on the role of four specialized  allied soldiers as they come together to  form a team on the multiplayer side the  focus is on the feeling of what it's  like to play as those special forces  soldiers in all combat scenarios  it sounds very much like a combination  of 2019's call of duty modern warfare  reboot and sledgehammer's call of duty  world war ii from 2017. in fact  sledgehammer says vanguard uses an  upgraded version of the modern warfare  engine you play as elite soldiers but  they're not yet the tier 1 operators of  modern warfare as sledgehammer described  it the down the barrel experience of  fighting in vanguard will have you  feeling like a hammer rather than modern  warfare's scalpel a lot of that comes  down to having the powerful automatic  weapons of world war ii at your disposal  while it seems we'll have opportunities  for stealth gameplay at times a lot of  vanguard is going to be about hitting  the enemy hard and fast to overwhelm  them don't expect the house clearing  moments of modern warfare vanguard seems  like it'll be less controlled and a  little more chaotic  vanguard's single player campaign  follows four characters each from a  different allied nation on their journey  to become the first special forces team  sledgehammer says the game is rooted in  history but not beholden to history so  this is a fictionalized story based on  some real people and events it's also  not linked to the story of call of duty  world war ii each of the main characters  is inspired by actual soldiers who  fought for the allies and the battles  they took part in sledgehammer says that  while working with historians on the  game the team focused on tide turning  battles and moments where individuals or  groups of soldiers had a major effect on  the war effort we saw a bit of the  campaign in action in which players took  on the role of sergeant arthur kingsley  the eventual leader of your special  forces team kingsley is a paratrooper in  the british sixth airborne division who  takes part in operation tonga in which  paratroopers jumped into normandy the  night before the allied invasion on  d-day his jump goes very badly as german  anti-aircraft guns pummel the british  planes and his shoot catches fire  kingsley manages to pull his reserve  chute just as he lands and nearly drowns  as he crashes into a pond losing his  rifle from there kingsley has to avoid  german patrols sneaking through the  darkened french countryside we saw the  usual call of duty blending of hands-off  cinematics and gameplay with kingsley  eventually finding a weapon and fighting  off german soldiers in a farmhouse the  whole portion highlighted the chaotic  high-stakes feel we can expect from  vanguard's missions there will be the  usual blend of stealth and tactical play  but these are turning points in the war  and sledgehammer wants to get across the  stakes and fear as well as the feeling  that you can also smash through the  enemy forces  sledgehammer said it's going for a  filmic blockbuster feel with vanguard  and the operation tonga level certainly  gave that impression the entire level  was intense with kingsley spending most  of it on the run hiding from enemies and  with very little ammo sledgehammer also  said that you'll have regenerating  health as you play health packs are gone  this time it seems likely we can expect  a similar approach from the rest of the  campaign you'll play as each member of  the team as they fight through battles  on different fronts of the war before  they finally come together as american  fighter pilot jack wade you'll fly in  the battle of midway before being shot  down over the solomon islands and  joining the 93rd infantry division  paulina petrova is a russian sniper who  you'll play during the battle of  stalingrad she's not just a deadly  sharpshooter but also an inspiration to  the russian people finally australian  lucas riggs fights in the north african  battle of el alamine disrupting the  enemy supply lines to help stop the  german tank division fighting there  eventually the team will come together  for a mission in berlin near the end of  the war  the allies have picked up intelligence  about something called operation phoenix  the team led by kingsley are sent to  infiltrate berlin find out what  operation phoenix is and try to stop it  sledgehammer also gave us some quick  facts about vanguard's multiplayer  offerings which sound like they'll  include some significant shifts from  other call of duty games the biggest new  item is champion hill mode which  sledgehammer described as being a bit of  a mix of battle royale and modern  warfare's gunfight mode eight teams face  off to be the last team standing on a  single map vanguard will also include  maps and game modes that will change the  combat pacing of your battles some modes  will be considered tactical which slows  down the speed of encounters requiring  you to be more methodical and careful  and where every bullet matters  on the other hand blitz games will pack  as many players into a map as it can  reasonably withstand creating a faster  more chaotic game that's high risk high  reward there will also be standard game  types which sound like they'll have a  more classic call of duty feel  firing up multiplayer from quick play  you might play through all three  experiences back to back you'll also be  able to set filters so you just get the  types of matches that you want vanguard  will launch with 20 multiplayer maps 16  of which will be six v6 maps with the  other four being two v2 maps expect  these maps to feel different from other  call of duty games going back to the  idea that you're a hammer and not a  scalpel maps will feature a lot more  destructibility than call of duty games  in the past where you won't just have  the ability to shoot other players  through certain pieces of cover or walls  but you'll actually be able to destroy  walls to create new lines of sight or  pathways it's not quite the level of  destructibility of battlefield games but  more like rainbow six siege where you  can alter certain places on the map to  create temporary advantages  expect multiplayer matches to shift as  they get more and more destroyed we  didn't get too much else in the way of  details about multiplayer but we do know  that elements like the gunsmith are  coming back along with additional  customizations like ballistics and ammo  types sledgehammer said it will reveal  more details in an upcoming multiplayer  showcase  in addition to the usual campaign and  multiplayer vanguard will also have its  own zombies mode which is being  developed by treyarch  the mode will act as a prequel to the  zombies mode in black ops cold war so  it'll operate in the same universe with  more zombie's lore and connections to  the story expect some alterations and  improvements to the core gameplay though  finally vanguard is also getting a new  warzone map developed by raven software  it uses the same tech as the rest of  vanguard so the guns and mechanics will  feel the same when switching between  vanguard's other modes and its warzone  map all of warzone's different  iterations will be connected through a  new metaverse sledgehammer says and  raven is also working on new anti-cheap  measures to improve the game  expect the usual live game features to  kick off when vanguard launches as well  sledgehammer says there's a huge  calendar of free seasonal content  planned and while it didn't give any  specifics it sounds like you can expect  elements of the campaign narrative to  carry forward with seasonal gameplay  just like in other recent call of duty  games as well as new multiplayer  offerings the last thing we know is the  release date november 5th 2021  we will have plenty more coverage of  call of duty vanguard ahead of its  release so be sure to stay tuned to  gamespot  [Music]  you
 

